---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="What personal data VigilOps collects and how it is used.">
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data {company.legalName} ("we") collects through vigilops.cloud and paid plans, and
    what we do with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Self-hosted VigilOps</h2>
  <p>
    The VigilOps software runs on your own servers. It does not send your server data, logs or backups to us. It sends data
    only to the services you configure yourself (for example Telegram, your storage bucket, or an AI provider), under those
    providers' terms. Once a day it checks GitHub for new releases; that request contains no information about your server.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect when you buy a plan</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and email address, to provide support and send account emails.</li>
    <li>
      Payment details, which are collected and processed by our payment provider Bachs. We receive confirmation of payment
      and subscription status, not your full card details.
    </li>
    <li>Anything you send us in support conversations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which processes basic request data such as IP addresses to deliver and protect the site.
    We do not use advertising trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account and billing records for as long as you are a customer and afterwards as long as the law requires for tax
    and accounting. You can ask us to delete other data at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it, by emailing
    <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
